course: dictionary
lesson: 10407
title: Tricycle and the tri- word family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tricycle is a small bike with three wheels, one at the front and two at the back. Its name gives you a clue: tri- means three, as in triangle and tripod, so a tricycle has three wheels.
explain: The word family helps you remember. Bi- means two, so a bicycle has 2 wheels. «A bicycle has 2 wheels, a tricycle 3, a car 4, and a usual train carriage 8.» Each word tells you the number of wheels.
explain: Tricycles are easy to balance, so toddlers ride them in the park or at preschool. Some grown-ups ride big ones to carry goods. When you see tri- in a new word, stop and ask: does this mean three?
fact: A tricycle is a small bike with three wheels: one at the front and two at the back.
fact: Tri- means three, as in triangle, tripod and tricycle.
fact: Bi- means two, as in bicycle.
fact: «Trike» is a short form of tricycle, used in everyday talk.
fact: Tricycles are easy to balance, so young children learn to ride them first.
exercise: How many wheels does a tricycle have? | Four | *Three | One | Two
exercise: «A bicycle has 2 wheels, a tricycle 3, a car 4.» Which vehicle has the most wheels? | *A car | A tricycle | They all have the same | A bicycle
exercise: What does the tri- in tricycle mean? | *Three | One | Four | Two
test: «4 bicycles, 2 tricycles and 3 unicycles» have how many wheels in total? | 9 | 24 | *17 | 14
test: «If all were bicycles, there would be 24 wheels; 5 wheels are left over.» How many tricycles are there? | *5 | 3 | 2 | 7
exam: «7 cycles with 17 wheels» means how many tricycles, if the rest are bicycles? | *3 | 14 | 7 | 4
